Open the Server Manager:
  Click the Start button, then search for Server Manager, and open it.

Add Roles and Features (if RD Licensing isn’t already installed):
  In Server Manager, click Manage > Add Roles and Features.
  Choose Role-based or feature-based installation.
  On the Server Roles screen, select Remote Desktop Services, then click Next.
  In the Role Services section, select Remote Desktop Licensing, then follow the prompts to complete the installation.

Open RD Licensing Manager:
  Press Win + R to open the Run dialog box.
  Type licmgr.exe and press Enter.
  This opens the RD Licensing Manager.

Manage Licenses:
  Once in the RD Licensing Manager, you can install and manage Remote Desktop licenses, activate the RD license server, and perform related tasks.

>>> STEPS TO OPEN RD LICENSING MANAGER VIA SERVER MANAGER:

Open Server Manager:
  Click the Start button and search for Server Manager. Select and open it.

Navigate to Remote Desktop Services:
  In Server Manager, on the left-hand side, click on Remote Desktop Services.

Open RD Licensing Manager:
  In the Remote Desktop Services section, under Overview, look for the option RD Licensing.
  Under Licensing, click RD Licensing Manager.

This will open the RD Licensing Manager.
